        "label": "Build the request that starts a seller's payment setup",
        "job": "Build, without sending it, the payment provider (Stripe) request that starts a seller's payment setup and gets their hosted onboarding link, or any other request the folder's operation map names",
        "description": "Calls buildStripeHttpRequest (tools/shared-code/src/build-provider-request.mjs) with the input: operation_id names one row of tools/shared-code/src/provider-operation-map.json (operation:create-connected-account and operation:create-account-link start a seller's setup and its hosted onboarding link; the map has every other operation too), input_facts holds what the request says (operation_subject becomes the form-encoded body of a write or the query of a search, provider_object_ref fills the address, acting_account the Stripe-Account header where the row declares it; a subject id becomes client_reference_id), idempotency_key becomes the Idempotency-Key header of a write, api_version_policy the Stripe-Version (the map's current version when left out) and required_credential_ref the name of the key a sender would use (credential-class:stripe-restricted-key when left out). Answers the finished request: method, url, headers, body, auth { scheme, credential_ref } and api_version. It holds and reads no key, puts no Authorization header on the request, sends nothing and moves no money: the request is for a sender (or a person) to look at first. Refuses an operation the map does not name and a missing provider_object_ref where the address needs one. The old screen also sent the request with the seller's own key and took the seller to the onboarding page the answer names; this run does neither.",
